WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.032
Missing data is not only a technical problem.

00:00:03.032 --> 00:00:05.262
It is a decision problem.

00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:11.652
We need to understand why a value is missing and what that absence means for the analysis.

00:00:11.652 --> 00:00:18.812
In this teaching example, a missing city is replaced with the label Unknown, while a missing amount is filled using the

00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:22.072
median of the available amounts.

00:00:22.072 --> 00:00:26.398
These are two different strategies because the columns have different meanings.

00:00:26.848 --> 00:00:29.860
Median filling is not a universal rule.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.335
In another project, dropping the row, preserving the missing value, using a domain-specific default,

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:42.140
or building a separate missing indicator could be more appropriate.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.879
The correct choice depends on the question and the data-generating process.
